  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates lotteries based on adjusted probabilities for outcomes with probabilities below 20%. In Lottery B, the outcome of 0 Euros occurs with 1% probability, which is less than 20%, so its probability is increased by 10 percentage points to 11%. The other outcomes in Lottery B (2500 Euros at 33% and 2400 Euros at 66%) are above or equal to 20%, so their probabilities remain unchanged. In Lottery A, all outcomes are certain (100% probability), so no adjustments are made. The reason then computes a weighted sum of outcomes using the adjusted probabilities and prefers the lottery with the higher sum. This reason is applicable to the decision problem because it involves outcomes with probabilities below 20% (specifically, the 1% chance of 0 Euros in Lottery B), and the necessary probabilities and outcomes are available.",
